Here is a complete, working solution using **Node.js** and **Express**. It handles file uploads, generates a unique download link, protects the download with a password (hashed using `bcrypt`), and provides a clean UI.

---

### Step 1: Project Setup

1. Create a new folder on your computer and open a terminal inside it:
   ```bash
   mkdir file-share-app
   cd file-share-app
   ```
2. Initialize a Node.js project:
   ```bash
   npm init -y
   ```
3. Install the required dependencies:
   ```bash
   npm install express multer bcryptjs uuid
   ```

---

### Step 2: Create the Server (`server.js`)

Create a file named `server.js` and paste the following code:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const multer = require('multer');
const bcrypt = require('bcryptjs');
const { v4: uuidv4 } = require('uuid');
const path = require('path');
const fs = require('fs');

const app = express();
const PORT = 3000;

// Ensure uploads folder exists
const uploadDir = path.join(__dirname, 'uploads');
if (!fs.existsSync(uploadDir)) {
  fs.mkdirSync(uploadDir);
}

// Multer storage configuration
const storage = multer.diskStorage({
  destination: (req, file, cb) => cb(null, 'uploads/'),
  filename: (req, file, cb) => cb(null, Date.now() + '-' + file.originalname)
});
const upload = multer({ storage });

// In-memory file database (for production, use MongoDB or SQLite)
const fileDB = new Map();

// Middleware
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true }));
app.use(express.json());

// 1. Home / Upload Page
app.get('/', (req, res) => {
  res.send(`
    <!DOCTYPE html>
    <html lang="en">
    <head>
      <meta charset="UTF-8">
      <title>Share a File</title>
      <style>
        body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 90vh; background: #f4f4f9; margin: 0; }
        .card { background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); width: 350px; }
        input, button { width: 100%; margin: 8px 0; padding: 10px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        button { background: #0066cc; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; }
        button:hover { background: #0052a3; }
      </style>
    </head>
    <body>
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Upload & Protect</h2>
        <form action="/upload" method="POST" enctype="multipart/form-data">
          <label>Choose File:</label>
          <input type="file" name="file" required />

          <label>Set Password:</label>
          <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Enter password" required />

          <button type="submit">Upload & Get Link</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </body>
    </html>
  `);
});

// 2. Handle File Upload
app.post('/upload', upload.single('file'), async (req, res) => {
  if (!req.file || !req.body.password) {
    return res.status(400).send('File and password are required.');
  }

  // Hash the password
  const hashedPassword = await bcrypt.hash(req.body.password, 10);
  const fileId = uuidv4();

  // Save metadata
  fileDB.set(fileId, {
    originalName: req.file.originalname,
    filePath: req.file.path,
    passwordHash: hashedPassword
  });

  const downloadLink = `${req.protocol}://${req.get('host')}/file/${fileId}`;

  res.send(`
    <body style="font-family: system-ui; text-align: center; margin-top: 10%;">
      <h2>File Uploaded Successfully!</h2>
      <p>Share this link with your friends:</p>
      <p><a href="${downloadLink}" target="_blank">${downloadLink}</a></p>
      <a href="/">Upload another file</a>
    </body>
  `);
});

// 3. Password Verification Page
app.get('/file/:id', (req, res) => {
  const file = fileDB.get(req.params.id);
  if (!file) return res.status(404).send('File not found or expired.');

  res.send(`
    <!DOCTYPE html>
    <html lang="en">
    <head>
      <meta charset="UTF-8">
      <title>Download Protected File</title>
      <style>
        body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; display: grid; place-items: center; min-height: 90vh; background: #f4f4f9; margin: 0; }
        .card { background: white; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); width: 350px; text-align: center; }
        input, button { width: 100%; margin: 8px 0; padding: 10px; box-sizing: border-box; }
        button { background: #28a745; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; }
        button:hover { background: #218838; }
      </style>
    </head>
    <body>
      <div class="card">
        <h2>Protected File</h2>
        <p>File: <strong>${file.originalName}</strong></p>
        <form action="/file/${req.params.id}/download" method="POST">
          <input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Enter password to unlock" required />
          <button type="submit">Unlock & Download</button>
        </form>
      </div>
    </body>
    </html>
  `);
});

// 4. Validate Password & Trigger Download
app.post('/file/:id/download', async (req, res) => {
  const file = fileDB.get(req.params.id);
  if (!file) return res.status(404).send('File not found or expired.');

  const isMatch = await bcrypt.compare(req.body.password, file.passwordHash);

  if (isMatch) {
    // Send the file with its original name
    res.download(path.resolve(file.filePath), file.originalName);
  } else {
    res.status(401).send(`
      <body style="font-family: system-ui; text-align: center; margin-top: 10%;">
        <h3 style="color: red;">Incorrect password!</h3>
        <a href="/file/${req.params.id}">Try again</a>
      </body>
    `);
  }
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Server running at http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

---

### Step 3: Run the Application

Run the server using Node:

```bash
node server.js
```

1. Open your browser and go to `http://localhost:3000`.
2. Choose a file, enter a password, and click **Upload & Get Link**.
3. Copy the generated link (e.g., `http://localhost:3000/file/...`).
4. Paste the link into a private/incognito window to test entering the correct and incorrect passwords.

---

### Optional Next Steps (For Production)
* **Hosting:** You can deploy this easily to platforms like **Render**, **Railway**, or **Fly.io**.
* **Persistence:** Currently, file references are stored in an in-memory `Map` (they reset when the server restarts). For persistent storage, swap the map with **SQLite** or **PostgreSQL**.
* **Auto-deletion:** To prevent server disk clutter, add `fs.unlinkSync(file.filePath)` combined with `setTimeout` to automatically delete files after 24 hours.

